<title>FRANCE: French December unemployment falls, rate 12.7 pct.</title>
<headline>French December unemployment falls, rate 12.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The seasonally adjusted number of people unemployed in France in December fell by 29,000, or 0.9 percent, from November to 3,092,500 Labour Ministry data showed.</p>
<p>The jobless rate, based on International Labour Organisation (ILO) criteria, which exclude jobseekers who did any work, was unchanged at a record 12.7 percent.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-Dec   month-on-month year-on-year</p>
<p> Jobless rate (ILO)	 12.7 pct  -0.0 pctge pt   1.0 pctge pt</p>
<p> Unemployment		3,092,500    -0.9 pct	    2.9 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment (ILO)	3,248,000    -0.3 pct	    9.2 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		  206,300     3.9 pct	   20.9 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations 352,400    -0.9 pct	    1.1 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits    356,100     1.3 pct	    n/a</p>
<p> Men under 25		  286,300    -2.1 pct	   2.4 pct</p>
<p> Women under 25		323,200    -2.6 pct	  -1.1 pct</p>
<p> Men between 25 and 49   1,046,600    -0.5 pct	   4.5 pct</p>
<p> Women between 25 and 49 1,062,100    -0.7 pct	   1.4 pct</p>
<p> Men 50 and over	     215,200    -0.2 pct	   6.7 pct</p>
<p> Women 50 and over	   159,100    -0.7 pct	   7.1 pct</p>
<p> Redundancy		    28,394	n/a		 6.5 pct</p>
<p> Jobless for over 12 mos 1,082,800    -0.2 pct	   2.2 pct</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
